{
  "from": "October 2026",
  "to": "November 2026",
  "fromUrl": "https://billionairepotential-pixel.github.io/the-vault/",
  "assessment": [
    "November was an interaction pass, not a rebuild, for most of the collection. Every one of the 20 decks changed, but most swaps trade greedy cards (Pot of Desires and Prosperity, Card Scanner, Upstart Goblin) and Ghost Belle for hand traps and board breakers. The real rebuilds were Synchron, Runick, Gren Maju, Lunalight and Ryu-Ge Mitsurugi, and on November 17 Metalmorph, which traded its Fiendsmith engine for Branded.",
    "The result is a collection that is much better at going second without getting any less consistent. The top four didn't move. The biggest climbs were Metalmorph (ten places, to #6), Ryu-Ge Mitsurugi (seven) and White Forest (three). Horus Mitsurugi, Earthbound Resonator and Swordsoul Tenyi each slipped five places, though all three scored about the same or better: the decks around them improved more."
  ],
  "watch": "Still the soft spots: Lunalight and Radiant Typhoon run the fewest interaction pieces (11), Dinomorphia is only 15% to see a breaker going second, Swordsoul Tenyi has the fewest one-card starters (6), and Spright has the highest brick rate (8.4%).",
